WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — satb-harness (90s) Narrator Mia

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.386
First, changing the wrapper around an AI model

2
00:00:03.386 --> 00:00:06.518
can swing scores as much as swapping the model.

3
00:00:07.018 --> 00:00:11.366
Second, this test harness locks prompts, memory trimming,

4
00:00:11.366 --> 00:00:15.027
and tools so every AI takes the exact same exam.

5
00:00:15.527 --> 00:00:17.866
Third, across five computer types,

6
00:00:17.866 --> 00:00:23.646
it separates real board sensors from chip counters and blocks noisy power estimates.

7
00:00:24.146 --> 00:00:28.526
Imagine timing sprinters on tracks of different lengths and then guessing

8
00:00:28.526 --> 00:00:32.845
their calorie burn by shoe size. That happens whenever AI benchmarks mix

9
00:00:32.845 --> 00:00:38.244
different history-trimming wrappers and split shared server watts by processor time alone.

10
00:00:38.744 --> 00:00:43.540
Our sequential Rust harness fixes six safe workspace tools, trims old outputs

11
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.896
above eighty percent window capacity using zero hidden model calls, hashes a five-part

12
00:00:48.896 --> 00:00:55.063
system fingerprint, and routes external command-line coding agents through one audited local proxy.

13
00:00:55.563 --> 00:01:01.611
Across Apple Silicon, Tegra circuit-board power shunts, two Linux workstations, and bare-metal Windows

14
00:01:01.611 --> 00:01:06.651
eleven, replay transcripts matched to the exact byte across twelve checks, while live

15
00:01:06.651 --> 00:01:11.750
endpoint probes caught cloud models drifting even when temperature was locked to zero.

16
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:19.544
Physical board shunt joules, built-in chip counters, and logical token counts never get blended into one fuzzy number,

17
00:01:19.544 --> 00:01:25.231
and automatic drift checks withhold net attribution whenever background jobs share the host.
